---
// HostCardMock: a faithful static mock of the Dashboard card on an LT Info monitoring
// program page (monitoring.laketahoeinfo.org/monitoring-programs/<id>). Spikes and QA
// pages wrap an embed body in it to see the embed the way the host frames it. It is
// never shipped inside an embed: the real host draws this card around the iframe.
//
// Values are read from the host's own stylesheet (styles-*.css on
// monitoring.laketahoeinfo.org, Nov. 5, 2026) and its Angular template, where the card is
// <div class="card"><div class="card-header flex"><span class="card-title">Dashboard</span>
// <span class="card-header-actions">...</span></div><div class="card-body">...</div></div>.
// The host names its own CSS custom properties below; they are the HOST's variables, not
// Ecology tokens, and are written without the leading dashes so the hub's token scanner
// does not read them as token uses:
//   .card          border 1px solid the host's card-border-color variable (#efefef), radius
//                  .25rem, no background of its own (the page shows through at the corners)
//   .card-header   padding .5rem .75rem, background from the host's card-header-bg-color
//                  variable, border-bottom 1px solid its card-header-border-color variable,
//                  white, 700, uppercase; .flex lays the title and the Fullscreen control out
//                  as a row. The stylesheet defaults both variables to #969eac; the Monitoring
//                  Dashboard sets them at runtime, and the live program page computes #789440
//                  for the header and #dddddd for the border-bottom (read with
//                  getComputedStyle on Nov. 5, 2026)
//   .card-title    font-size from the host's type-size-300 variable = clamp(.87rem, .74rem +
//                  .62vw, 1.13rem), 700, no margin; so about 18 px at 980 px and wider,
//                  13.9 px at 375 px
//   .card-body     padding from the host's spacing-500 and spacing-600 variables = 1.5rem
//                  2rem, background from its card-body-bg-color variable (#f7f7f7)
//   body           Lexend Deca, 16 px, line-height 1.4; card text #333333
// The Fullscreen control in the header is omitted: it is the host's behavior, not chrome
// the embed has to fit.
//
// mon-lego-checked: no esa-* fits because this is HOST chrome (the host's card), not an
// Ecology surface. It reproduces the host's literal hex values and pixel sizes on purpose,
// so it reads none of the Ecology tokens that a theme could move; HostCardMock is the
// reusable home for that chrome.
// bcn-lego-checked: same justification, written as the literal the spoke-kit component-first
// hook reads (check-component-first.mjs, line 44). The class name mon-host-card matches its
// card rule, and esa-card is the wrong answer because the mock must reproduce the host's
// card, not the Ecology one. Kept in the frontmatter so it does not ship in the HTML.
interface Props {
  /** The card title as the host renders it: uppercase, white, 700, host type-size-300. */
  title?: string;
}
const { title = 'Dashboard' } = Astro.props;
---
<!-- mon-lego-checked: host chrome, not an Ecology component. Literal LT Info hex values are intentional; see the frontmatter note. -->
<section class="mon-host-card">
  <header class="mon-host-card__header">
    <h2 class="mon-host-card__title">{title}</h2>
  </header>
  <div class="mon-host-card__body">
    <slot />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Host chrome. Every value below is read from monitoring.laketahoeinfo.org's stylesheet
     and is a literal by design: this block must not follow the spoke theme, or the mock
     stops being a reference to compare the theme against. */
  .mon-host-card {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 980px;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-family: 'Lexend Deca', system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #333333;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid #efefef;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* .card-header.flex on the host. */
  .mon-host-card__header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    background: #789440;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dddddd;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* .card-title on the host: its type-size-300 variable, 700, no margin. */
  .mon-host-card__title {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: clamp(0.87rem, 0.74rem + 0.62vw, 1.13rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: inherit;
  }

  /* .card-body on the host: its spacing-500 and spacing-600 variables. */
  .mon-host-card__body {
    min-width: 0;
    background: #f7f7f7;
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }
</style>
